From ad81dd59f1559dfea74629d4133d75b168047c55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:03:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] publish prepare: bounded read pacing and HTTP-429-only
 retries (ROOT-READ-PACING)

Root's live read-only prepare died on mainnet.base.org eth_maxPriorityFeePerGas HTTP 429.
One paced transport per prepare: per provider one start per 250 ms; HTTP 429 only, at most
3 retries per request, Retry-After <= 5 s honoured (longer refuses), else 0.5/1/2 s backoff;
other errors fail at once. Finite budgets: 80 attempts, 60 s; the agreed block must be at
most 60 s old when the plan is written (stale refuses) and the time budget may never exceed
the freshness window. Two-RPC agreement and every guard, the request (calldata 13e5a6f4) and
the WASM unchanged. Tests: transport 8/8 on a discrete-event fake clock, anvil 10/10,
mutants 23/23.
